#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f149f8ef-dd7f-5f65-928e-534e1541f9b2" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Rational Expressions with a Single Common Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "4fba84c9-6c0f-51cd-b5f2-8b469bd8346f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5135" :question/problem "What is the result of dividing $\\dfrac 3 x$ by $\\dfrac y {6x^2}?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\div \\dfrac{y}{6x^2},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\div  \\dfrac y {6x^2} &=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\cdot  \\dfrac {6x^2} y &=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x^2} {xy}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x^\\cancel{2}} {\\cancel{x}y}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x} {y}&\t\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $x$ in the numerator and denominator."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7614a05-f221-5fda-b491-6893f44a1a5f" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Rational Expressions with Multiple Common Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "fa6bbedb-654a-58a5-8fcf-3bb0fd038160" :question/math-academy-id "e-5136" :question/problem "Given that $\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  =x$ and $\\dfrac {1+b}{5b^2} =y ,$ then what is $x \\div y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $x \\div y,$ i.e., \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{a}^{2}(1+b)}{3b} & ÷\\frac{1+b}{5{b}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  \\div  \\dfrac{1+b}{5b^2}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {5b^2} {1+b}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2\\cancel{(1+b)}} {3\\cancel{b}}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {5b^{\\cancel{2}}} {\\cancel{1+b}}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {10a^2b} {3}  \n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "993a1649-c534-5a08-805f-3388c2f83b20" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Rational Expressions with No Common Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "dd8b5378-4da1-5955-a566-f84ef0cecb28" :question/math-academy-id "e-5206" :question/problem "What is the result of dividing $\\dfrac 3 x$ by $\\dfrac {5}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\div \\dfrac{5}{y},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\div  \\dfrac 5 y&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\cdot  \\dfrac y 5&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {3y} {5x}\t\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc27633-cfde-532e-a38a-28d195fd2a5b" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Rational Expressions and Simplifying the Result by Factoring"}] :question/id #uuid "3fd58494-e5ee-5dc7-af3c-959888f59627" :question/math-academy-id "e-5207" :question/problem "Given that $\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  =x$ and $\\dfrac {2a} {14b^2}=y,$ then what is $x \\div y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  &\\div  \\dfrac {2a} {14b^2},\n\t}\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \\div  \\dfrac {2a} {14b^2}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \\cdot \\dfrac {14b^2} {2a}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a(a^2 - 5)} {7b}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {2b \\cdot 7b} {2a}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {\\cancel{2a}(a^2 - 5)} {\\cancel{7b}}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {2b \\cdot \\cancel{7b}} {\\cancel{2a}}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2b(a^2 - 5)} 1 &=\\\n\t\t2a^2b - 10b &\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "993a1649-c534-5a08-805f-3388c2f83b20" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Rational Expressions with No Common Factors"}] :